---
id: layout
course: test
title: Room on the board
cover: optional
source: A short test of gaps and a second column on the board. Not a lesson.
---
title: Two problems on one board
say: Here is the first problem.
write p1: \frac{d}{dx}\,(3x+1)^5
write a1: = 5(3x+1)^4 \cdot 3
write b1: = 15(3x+1)^4
say: A gap sets the second problem apart, and the first one stays up.
gap:
write p2: \frac{d}{dx}\,\sin(x^2)
write a2: = \cos(x^2) \cdot 2x
say: There is room beside the first problem, so notes can go there.
column: right beside p1
note n1: outside: something to the fifth
note n2: inside: 3x + 1
say: And writing carries on down the first column.
column: left
note c: Both use the chain rule.
say: That is the end of the test.
